What:		/sys/kernel/mm/ashmem/
Date:		Nov 2024
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		/sys/kernel/mm/ashmem/ contains a single node that can be used
		to enable memfd compatibility mode for the ashmem driver.

		This causes the ashmem driver to allocate memfds and act as a
		thin wrapper around them.

What:		/sys/kernel/mm/ashmem/memfd_compat_enable
Date:		Nov 2024
Contact:	Isaac J. Manjarres <isaacmanjarres@google.com>
Description:
		Can be read to determine what mode the ashmem driver is
		operating in.

		A value of 0 indicates that the driver is operating in legacy
		mode.

		A value of 1 indicates that the driver is operating in memfd
		compatible mode, which causes it to allocate memfds each time
		/dev/ashmem is opened.

		Writing a value of 1 to the node enables memfd compatible mode.
		The write will only take effect if no ashmem buffers have been
		allocated beforehand.
